    <DataNode elementId="AT2G45970-MONOMER" textLabel="Cytochrome P450 86A8" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O80823" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">CYP86A8 hydroxylates fatty acids of various chain lengths, but the highest activity was observed with palmitate and oleate as substrates |CITS: [11493698]|. Arabidopsis mutants in CYP86A8 displayed defects in cuticle formation, which indicated a physiological role of CYP86A8 in cutin biosynthesis |CITS: [11493698]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G45970-MONOMER" />
